    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2a4a63cd_ab87df98",
        "filename": "framework/java/android/bluetooth/BluetoothLeBroadcast.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 667,
      "author": {
        "id": 1928988
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-01T09:51:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Changing group settings will require BIG teardown and new BIG creation since this is the only way to change the number of BISes (subgroups). In such case the only thing that makes it different from stopping and starting a new broadcast is that the broadcastId stays the same. Is that really what we want to do here?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 666,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 667,
        "endChar": 85
      },
      "revId": "2b5e25f6bb9f22212233b7144c28376ed848b6ab",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "653c3091_af7566d7",
        "filename": "framework/java/android/bluetooth/BluetoothLeBroadcast.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 667,
      "author": {
        "id": 1981586
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-01T16:53:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The intent behind this updateBroadcast change is to make API ready to update the whole BIG, e.g. multi contentMeta at the same time, and keep aligned with the startBroadcast change. Later we can introduce some logics in the internal service, e.g. whether we\u0027d support changing the num of subgroups in updateBroadcast. In current design, only one subgroup is supported anyways, but we\u0027d like to make the API expandable first.",
      "parentUuid": "2a4a63cd_ab87df98",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 666,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 667,
        "endChar": 85
      },
      "revId": "2b5e25f6bb9f22212233b7144c28376ed848b6ab",
